infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Choreography vs orchestration: the real tradeoff
  desc Both couple — they just couple different things differently
  compares
    - label Choreography
      children
        - label Flow
          desc Implicit, emergent across all subscriptions
        - label Coupling
          desc To the event schema, not to each other
        - label Visibility
          desc Invisible — read every subscription to trace
        - label New cross-cutting rule
          desc No owner — days to find where to change
        - label Best fit
          desc Simple, stable flows between few services
    - label Orchestration
      children
        - label Flow
          desc Explicit — one process-manager owns the sequence
        - label Coupling
          desc To the orchestrator — a central coupling hub
        - label Visibility
          desc Visible — audit, test, change in one place
        - label New cross-cutting rule
          desc One place to change — the OrderSaga
        - label Best fit
          desc Complex, frequently-changing transactions
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
